<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arte di Calimala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arte di Calimala was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> of cloth merchants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, named after the street where its members had their shops. The first in prestige of the city's seven major guilds, it imported woollen cloth from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, finished and dyed it, and sold it across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. It also supervised major works such as the Baptistery of Florence and its bronze doors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arte-di-calimala.jpg" alt="Arte di Calimala" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utente:Elenasan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stemma_dell%27arte_di_Calimala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
